{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98993","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98993/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98993/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98993/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98993","id":2646213977,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc6dugVZ","number":98993,"title":"Visibility ranges ignored when casting shadows under Omni/Spot lights","user":{"login":"UltyX","id":12592569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTkyNTY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12592569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX","html_url":"https://github.com/UltyX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UltyX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2024-11-09T15:23:29Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T17:52:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\r\n\r\n4.3 stable, 4.4dev4\r\n\r\n### System information\r\n\r\nLinux\r\n\r\n### Issue description\r\n\r\nUsing Visibility Range Begin and End to hide an Object always creates a shadow for OmniLight3D, even if the camera is far away and the Object becomes hidden by the set Visibility Range.  DirectionalLight3D only creates a shadow for the object if it was not hidden by Visibility Range.\r\n\r\nUse case:\r\nThis is an issue for me because I would like to keep using Visibility Range to hide a 3D objects Mesh so it only creates a shadow but is not visible to the user. There is no LightOccluder3D Node in Godot and setting the Mesh transparency = 1.0 has been a performance drain (I use many light blocker mesh instances)\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nSet a MeshInstance3D Visibility Range between 1.0 and 2.0 and zoom in and out with the camera and take note of the shadow on the floor (OmniLight3D = always shadow, DirectionalLight3D = shadow only if mesh is visible). The behavior is present in the editor and when running the project.\r\n\r\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\r\n\r\n\r\n[lightingtest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17688518/lightingtest.zip)\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98993/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98993/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}